<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-4f3ad234c8f24a6784176fa177b76d83" title="sat-c2-u24-eloquent.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>A</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;eloquent&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The closing speaker at the water-rights hearing was so eloquent that ranchers who had come to heckle stayed to shake her hand.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">Being effortlessly eloquent, the tour guide slid from Italian to German to English without ever dropping a single syllable.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">Marta was far too eloquent to speak at the awards banquet, so she simply nodded her thanks from her seat and passed the microphone on.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The patent&apos;s eloquent claims section runs to eleven dense pages of numbered sub-clauses that only three living attorneys can parse.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Eloquent means using language so movingly that it stirs the audience, so it&apos;s the correct answer because the speech turned hecklers into hand-shakers — the words did the moving, and the room&apos;s change of heart is the proof.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Eloquent means using language so fluently and movingly that it stirs the audience, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because sliding among three languages is multilingual skill — a talent for languages, not the power of what is said in any of them.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Eloquent means using language so fluently and movingly that it stirs the audience, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because someone &apos;too eloquent to speak&apos; is a contradiction — the word names a gift for speaking, not a reason to stay seated.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Eloquent means using language so fluently and movingly that it stirs the audience, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because eleven dense pages of sub-clauses that only three living attorneys can parse shut the audience out — impenetrable is not moving.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
